<title>USA: MacDermid acquires board fabrication unit.</title>
<headline>MacDermid acquires board fabrication unit.</headline>
<dateline>WATERBURY, Conn. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>MacDermid Inc said Thursday it had a definitive agreement to acquire the Board Fabrication division of Unilever Plc's National Starch and Chemical Co.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not immediately available, a MacDermic company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>National acquired the fabrication division as part of its purchase of Grace Specialty Polymers Business in May 1997.</p>
<p>MacDermid, a $300 million specialty chemical company that supplies to the printed circuit board manufacturing market, said it expects the deal to close in 30 days.</p>
<p>&quot;The addition of former Grace products and technical people will clearly position us as a leader in photoimaging in the PC market,&quot; a company statement said.</p>
</text>
